# Common Error-Namespace Convention — two leaves, an allocated code space, a blocking epistemics gate; PLACEMENT UNRATIFIED [SPEC:CXC-ERR-NAMESPACE]

> Every fleet emitter reports its own faults through the SAME two-namespace shape —
> `_error/<id>/register` (a periodic STATE bitfield, because silence is itself the death
> report) and `_error/<id>/event` (a retained EVENT per occurrence). One shared, allocated
> error-code space grows the same way [BP-TYPE-CODES] grows: seeded small, one allocation,
> never renumbered. Severity reaches the CAN arbitration id, not just the payload, so a
> critical fault out-arbitrates telemetry exactly when things go wrong. This spec DEPENDS ON
> the LOG_ENTRY retirement / namespace-mode collapse (`spec/01-composeio-bus-protocol.smd`
> §1.6.1, `spec/01-amendment-bus-extensions.smd` §2.4) — an error IS a retained event, and
> this convention falls out of that collapse's `kind x retention` model for free.

---

