## 4. Register-class taxonomy — 8 bits, class-ranged codes

### [CXC-ERR-TAXONOMY] The 8-bit register-class taxonomy — one bit per class, codes class-ranged, ONE-ALLOCATION-NEVER-RENUMBER

- taxonomy: an 8-bit bitfield, one bit per class, mirroring CANopen Error Register 1001h:

| Bit | Class | Code range |
|-----|-------|-----------|
| 0 | comms | 0x1n |
| 1 | config | 0x2n |
| 2 | plugin | 0x3n |
| 3 | identity | 0x4n |
| 4 | policy | 0x5n |
| 5 | resource | 0x6n |
| 6 | data | 0x7n |
| 7 | internal | 0xFn |

- discipline: codes are class-ranged (`0x1n` comms … `0xFn` internal) and
  ONE-ALLOCATION-NEVER-RENUMBERED — the identical discipline [BP-TYPE-CODES] applies to wire
  codes, applied here to fault codes. A hashed error code would collide and re-rank exactly like
  a hashed arbitration id would; allocation is sequential and permanent.
- seeded-small: the code space is SEEDED SMALL (15 codes, [CXC-ERR-SEED-V1]) and GROWS over
  time as real conditions get producers — see [CXC-ERR-GAPS] for what is deliberately NOT
  seeded yet.
- status: decided (taxonomy + discipline); ratified accept-all with the seed set
- provenance: david-ruling accept-all of the composeio-expert-distilled taxonomy, from a
  read-only sweep of the ComposeServer/ComposeBus implementation on origin/main (d95aee1)
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-ERR-NAMESPACE]
- see-also: [CXC-ERR-SEED-V1], [CXC-ERR-DEFERRED]

### [CXC-ERR-SEED-V1] The v1 seed set — 15 codes, one-per-class plus comms heavies plus the two criticals

- table: full v1 allocation. `fmi` follows J1939's Failure Mode Identifier convention.
  ⛔ **Evidence tier**: `code`/`name`/`class` are RATIFIED (David accept-all,
  `DEC-ERROR-CODE-SEED-SET-V1-2026-08-25`). `severity-default` is ratified ONLY for the two
  rows the DEC node calls out explicitly (0x21, 0x51 — deliberately fatal/latching; 0x70 — warn
  external-dispatch / critical unguarded-local). Every OTHER severity-default and every `fmi`
  value below is ARCHITECT-SYNTHESIS pending David's review, per
  [DX-INTERPRETATION-IS-AN-INFERENCE] — flagged, not silently promoted to ratified.

| Code | Name | Class | Severity (default) | FMI | Origin site | Meaning |
|------|------|-------|---------------------|-----|-------------|---------|
| 0x10 | LINK_DOWN | comms | warning | 5 | not independently re-grounded this pass — verify against the composeio-expert sweep before implementation | A comms link the node owns has gone down |
| 0x11 | BACKEND_UNREACHABLE | comms | warning | 9 | not independently re-grounded this pass — verify against the composeio-expert sweep before implementation | A configured backend (broker, bridge, hub) is unreachable |
| 0x12 | RX_FRAME_CORRUPT | comms | warning | 2 | not independently re-grounded this pass — verify against the composeio-expert sweep before implementation | A received frame failed its integrity check (CRC/checksum) |
| 0x13 | RX_FRAME_UNDECODABLE | comms | warning | 19 | not independently re-grounded this pass — verify against the composeio-expert sweep before implementation | A received frame parsed structurally but carried an unmappable/unallocated value |
| 0x20 | CONFIG_INVALID | config | critical | 13 | `python/composeio/config.py:291,509` — `ConfigError` raised from validation/compile | Config failed validation or compile |
| 0x21 | UNKNOWN_TRANSPORT_TYPE | config | critical — DELIBERATELY FATAL, register bit LATCHES | 31 | `python/composeio/transport_registry.py:94` — `f"unknown transport type {ttype!r}..."` | A configured transport `type:` has no registered factory |
| 0x30 | PLUGIN_PARKED | plugin | warning | 7 | not independently re-grounded this pass — ComposeServer's requires-floor parking, Phase-0 in progress ([CXC-CBK-KERNEL-PRIMITIVES]) — verify against sweep once `composeserver.py` standup lands | A plugin's resolved isolation floor is not yet satisfiable; it is parked, not started |
| 0x40 | NS_HASH_COLLISION | identity | critical | 2 | `python/composeio/ns_announce.py:600` — `"collision is still a collision; the first entry keeps it."` | Two distinct namespace names hashed to the same id; a receiver would confidently decode the wrong namespace |
| 0x41 | TOOL_NAME_COLLISION | identity | warning | 2 | not independently re-grounded this pass — MCP surface tool registration — verify against the composeio-expert sweep before implementation | Two MCP tools registered under the same name |
| 0x42 | NODE_ID_INVALID | identity | warning | 2 | not independently re-grounded this pass — verify against the composeio-expert sweep before implementation | An allocated node id (e.g. CAN `src`) is out of range or unassigned where required |
| 0x50 | PUBLISH_DENIED | policy | warning | 14 | `python/composeio/namespace.py:446` — publish-whitelist validation ([BP-EXT-ACCESS]) | A publish was rejected by the namespace's access-policy whitelist |
| 0x51 | UNSAFE_BIND_REFUSED | policy | critical — DELIBERATELY FATAL, register bit LATCHES | 14 | not independently re-grounded this pass — MCP connector bind-safety check — verify against the composeio-expert sweep before implementation | An MCP connector refused to bind because the bind would be unsafe |
| 0x60 | DEPENDENCY_MISSING | resource | warning | 31 | not independently re-grounded this pass — verify against the composeio-expert sweep before implementation | A required dependency (module, service, resource) is absent |
| 0x70 | ENGINE_VALUE_REJECTED | data | warning (external-dispatch: log+drop) — critical on the unguarded LOCAL path (can SIGABRT) | 2 | `python/composeio/state_engine.py:41` — `raise ValueError(f"Invalid value '{value}' for {self.engine_type} engine...")` | A published value failed the namespace's state-engine domain check |
| 0xF0 | SUBSCRIBER_CALLBACK_ERROR | internal | warning | 12 | `python/composeio/bus.py:281,1337` — `logger.error(f"Message callback error: {e}")` | A subscriber's callback raised while handling a delivered message |

- sigabrt-hazard: the 0x70-critical unguarded-local-path SIGABRT hazard (empty-string into a
  binary domain check) is dispatched to defect-investigator separately from this spec, per
  `DEC-ERROR-CODE-SEED-SET-V1-2026-08-25`.
- pre-integration-question: for every row marked "not independently re-grounded this pass," the
  exact file:line MUST be confirmed against the composeio-expert sweep (or re-grounded directly)
  before a producer is written against this table — see [DX-SPEC-CARRIES-ITS-EVIDENCE]. This is
  a deliberate EMPTY-marked gap, not a silent one.
- status: decided (code/name/class allocation); proposed (fmi values, non-called-out severities)
- provenance: david-ruling accept-all (code/name/class, from the composeio-expert sweep of
  origin/main d95aee1); architect-synthesis (fmi assignment, non-called-out severity defaults)
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-ERR-NAMESPACE]
- see-also: [CXC-ERR-TAXONOMY], [CXC-ERR-SEVERITY-DEFAULT], [CXC-ERR-DEFERRED]

### [CXC-ERR-DEFERRED] 16 deferred codes — allocate on need, do NOT pre-mint

- list: `0x14 TX_PAYLOAD_OVERSIZE`, `0x15 TX_QUEUE_OVERFLOW`, `0x16 RX_LOOP_ERROR`,
  `0x22 NS_DECL_CONTRADICTION`, `0x23 FRESHNESS_CLASS_INVALID`, `0x24 BRIDGE_ROUTE_INVALID`,
  `0x25 NS_PATTERN_INVALID`, `0x32 PLUGIN_STOP_ERROR`, `0x33 PLUGIN_DECL_INVALID`,
  `0x43 TENANT_EXISTS`, `0x52 BOUNDARY_VIOLATION`, `0x53 MCP_BINDING_VIOLATION`,
  `0x61 GLOBAL_TRANSPORT_DARK`, `0x71 VALUE_NOT_SERIALIZABLE`, `0x72 ENGINE_CONFIG_INVALID`,
  `0xF1 HOOK_ERROR`.
- rule: these names and code slots are RESERVED (nothing else may claim `0x14`, etc.) but NOT
  allocated to a live producer. Allocate one only when a real condition needs it — minting a
  code with no producer is exactly the aspirational-empty state [CXC-ERR-GAPS] warns against for
  CAN `/link`.
- status: decided (reservation); the codes themselves are dev-time/config-authoring faults or
  fine-grained variants folded into a v1 code's payload sub-reason until split out
- provenance: david-ruling accept-all
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-ERR-NAMESPACE]
- see-also: [CXC-ERR-SEED-V1], [CXC-ERR-GAPS]

